Before switching, \[V_C(0^-)=0\] Since the voltage across a capacitor cannot change instantaneously, \[V_C(0^+)=V_C(0^-)=0\] The capacitor current is \[i_C=C\frac{dV_C}{dt}\] <img src="img/6a7f6ffe5d4b6a1b.webp" loading="lazy" alt="" style="width:min(100%,192px)"> Applying KVL at \(t=0^+\), \[-1+V_C(0^+)+Ri_C(0^+)=0\] Substituting \(V_C(0^+)=0\) and \(i_C=C\dfrac{dV_C(0^+)}{dt}\), \[-1+RC\frac{dV_C(0^+)}{dt}=0\] Hence, \[RC\frac{dV_C(0^+)}{dt}=1\] \[\boxed{
\left.\frac{dV_C}{dt}\right|_{t=0^+}
=
\frac{1}{RC}
}\] Therefore, the correct answer is \[\boxed{\textbf{D. }\frac{1}{RC}}\]

