=
\frac{\text{slots}}{\text{poles}}
=
\frac{16}{4}
=
4\] \[\boxed{D}\] <div class="sol-block sol-keypoints"><div class="sol-block-title">Key points</div><ul><li>In double-layer winding, each slot contains two coil sides.</li><li>For single-turn coils, one coil has two conductors.</li><li>Pole pitch in slots is calculated as total slots divided by number of poles.</li></ul></div> <div class="sol-block sol-mistakes"><div class="sol-block-title">Mistakes to avoid</div><ul><li>Do not forget that double-layer winding has two coil sides per slot.</li><li>Use total slots, not total conductors, for calculating pole pitch.</li></ul></div>

